  "result": "NRS_484B_283_1b passed the gate (**OK**) on the sixth and last run: all 9 witnesses gave their expected verdicts and all 9 composed exception rules resolved. After that run I only changed comments in the two file headers; the harness re-runs the gate on the final files itself.\n\n**The rule** (`NRS_484B_283_1b.lean`):\n- **Who and when:** the subject is a pedestrian who, at this observation, is on a roadway and at the previous observation was on no roadway but on a sidewalk, safety zone or median. All nine exception rules must also not apply.\n- **The duty:** no vehicle may have a predicted closest approach to the pedestrian within the 3 s horizon, closer than the clearance distance, while being unable to stop. \"Unable to stop\" uses the record's stopping-distance test, rewritten in an equivalent form so the surface-dependent braking rate (ice, else wet, else dry) appears only once. With four copies, the gate hit a stack overflow.\n- **Narrowings:** none of my own; the formulas follow the record's reading.\n\n**The witnesses** (`NRS_484B_283_1b.lean` under `TrafficSpecWitness`): the five planned scenarios, plus four extra ones:\n- `branch_2`: on a wet road the pedestrian is too close, though on a dry road it would comply.\n- `branch_3`: the same on ice, against wet and dry.\n- `branch_4` and `branch_5`: the pedestrian steps off a safety zone or a median instead of a sidewalk.\n\n**Something the plan agent should check:** the planned scenes only reached \"violated\" or \"compliant\" once I put a marked crosswalk where the pedestrian steps off. Without it, one of the exceptions applied and every scene came back \"not applicable\". I wasn't allowed to read those rules, so I'm guessing it is one of the NRS 484B.287 rules about crossing outside a crosswalk. If so, this duty never applies to a pedestrian stepping off anywhere except a crosswalk. That fits how the statute is laid out, but it should be confirmed as intended. I noted this in `task_result.md`.\n\n`task_result.md` also covers what changed after each gate run and the choices the node left open.",
